Language English

Book Crypt Ordered No Keep Looped
	Page ExploreViaChapel
		Not Visible
		
		exploredCryptViaChapel = true
		Goto PlaceCrypt
	End Page ExploreViaChapel
	
	Page ExploreViaDungeonCave
		Not Visible
		
		exploredChapelViaDungeon = true
		Goto PlaceCrypt
	End Page
	
	Page PlaceCrypt
		Not Visible
		Triggered By @ExploreCryptViaDungeonCave
		
		Prolog "The cave continues into the darkness."
		Button "Look"
		
		Add TileCrypt
		Remove TokenExploreCryptViaDungeonCave
		
		Text """
			You walk forward a bit and realize the other part of the cave
			is a crypt containing above-ground vaults. The air is different, 
			even from the cave you have been in.
			
			Place the {c:TileCrypt} tile and discard this Sight token.
		"""
		
		If exploredCryptViaChapel Then Text """
			You peer into the darkspace but cannot see much. Move 1 space
			into the explored area.
			
			You eyes adjust quickly to the light.
			
			Place the {c:TileCrypt} tile and discard this Search token.
		"""
		
		Goto PlaceSearchPendant
	End Page PlaceCrypt
	
	Page PlaceSearchPendant
		Not Visible
		Add TokenSearchCryptPendant!
		
		Text """
			One of the vaults is open. You aren't sure you want to look inside.
			Place a Search token as indicated.
		"""
		
		If exploredCryptViaDungeonCave Then Goto PlaceExploreChapelViaCrypt
		Goto PlaceSearchHenry
	End Page PlaceSearchPendant

	Page PlaceExploreChapelViaCrypt
		Not Visible
		
		Add TokenSearchChapelViaCrypt!
		
		Text """
			Something about the wall seems... off. Place a Search token
			as indicated.
		"""
		Goto PlaceSearchHenry
	End Page PlaceExploreChapelViaCrypt
	
	Page PlaceSearchHenry
		Not Visible
		Text """
			The casket on the end looks much newer than the others. Place a
			Search token as indicated.
		"""
	End Page PlaceSearchHenry
	
	Page PlaceExit No Text
		Exit
	End Page PlaceExit
	
	Page SearchChapelViaCrypt
		Not Visible
		Triggered By @SearchChapelViaCrypt
		
		Prolog """
			The wall in front of you is smooth rock. Is that a cut?
		"""
		Button "Search"
		
		Text """
			You walk up to the wall and put your hands on it, moving around
			until you see it:  a razor-thin, rectangular cut into the rock. The
			cut is about the size of the other doors inside the house. Maybe
			this is a door too?
			
			A lot of time passes before you finally give up looking for...
			something. Become Stunned.
			
			Discard this Search token.
		"""
		
		Remove TokenSearchChapelViaCrypt
	End Page SearchChapelViaCrypt
	
	Page SearchPendant
		Not Visible
		Triggered By @SearchCryptPendant
		
		Prolog """
			The casket inside the vault is also open. You wonder what might have
			been interred with the body. And whether there is anything left
			after whatever descecration left the casket open.
		"""
		Button "Search"
		
		Remove TokenSearchCryptPendant
		
		Text """
			Mixed in with the bones, tattered clothing, and cobwebs are several
			pieces of junk jewelry, tarnished and of no value. But there is one
			piece that looks like it might be worth something. Gain the
			{c:QItemElderSignPendant} Common Item, then discard this Search
			token.
		"""
		
		Exit
	End Page SearchPendant
	
	Page SearchHenry
		Not Visible
		Triggered By @SearchCryptHenry
		
		Prolog """
			A brass plate on top of the casket looks like it has the name of the
			person inside. The letters dance and swim, much like the text in the
			{c:QItemOldJournal}.
			
			Only {c:EventChosenInvestigator} can read the inscription.
		"""
		Button "Search"
		
		Text """
			When you lean over to read it, the letters coalesce into the name
			and dates of the person inside. You read out loud:
			
			Here lies Henry Smythe\n
			Born 12 May, 1885 -- Died 31 October, 1915

			It seems your father died after stopping the ritual 10 years
			ago. You cannot remember him, but thinking about him lying dead
			three feet away makes your chest hurt.
			
			Remove this Search token.
		"""
		
		henryIsDead = true
		Remove TokenSearchChapelHenry
		Exit
	End Page SearchHenry
End Book Crypt